    "created_at": "2023-09-11T18:08:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-09-11T18:08:36Z",
    "body": "Can't find a good reference link, but this [patch discussion](https://linux-usb.vger.kernel.narkive.com/wSEOXlqR/patch-usb-composite-fix-bmaxpacketsize-for-superspeed) that pops up among first Google results is helpful:\r\n\r\n> For bMaxPacketSize0 we usually take what is specified in ep0->maxpacket.\r\nThis is fine in most cases, however on SuperSpeed bMaxPacketSize0\r\nspecifies the exponent instead of the actual size in bytes. The only\r\nvalid value on SS is 9 which denotes 512 bytes.",
